{"id":"word:hebrew:H408","type":"word","title":"אַל","subtitle":"H408 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"not (the qualified negation, used as a deprecative); once (Job 24:25) as a noun, nothing","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אַל (H408) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: adv.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 725 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אַל (ʼal) means not (the qualified negation, used as a deprecative); once (Job 24:25) as a noun, nothing First listed occurrence: 1Chr 16 22."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אַל","transliteration":"ʼal","pronunciation":"al","strong":"H408","lemmaId":"hebrew:H408","partOfSpeech":"adv","forms":["אַל","וְ/אַל","אַֽל","וְ/אַֽל","וְֽ/אַל"],"morphs":[["HTn",574],["HC/Tn",147],["HR",2],["HC/R",1],["HR/Tn",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"not (the qualified negation, used as a deprecative); once (Job 24:25) as a noun, nothing","usage":"nay, neither, + never, no, nor, not, nothing (worth), rather than.","full":"H408. al II. אַל adverb of negation (so Phoenician e.g. CIS i. 3, 4.5.8 , Biblical Aramaic, Sabean (DHM ZMG 1875, 596 ), and in the Ethiopic albo, is not ), denying however, not objectively as a fact (like לֹא οὐ ), but subjectively as a wish (like μή ), expressing therefore a deprecation or prohibition: a. ( a ) with a verb, which is then always an imperfect (never an imperative), by preference in the cohortative or jussive mood, where this is in use, and may be of any person or number; Gen 15:1 and often אַלתִּֿירָא fear not! 22:12 יָָֽדְךָ אַלתִּֿשְׁלַח put not forth thy hand, 37:27 אַלתְּֿהִיבֿוֺ וְיָדֵנוּ and let not our hand be upon him, 21:16 אַלאֶֿרְאֶה let me not look upon the death of the lad! Psa 25:2 אַלאֵֿבוֺשָׁה let me not be ashamed; with 1 plural (rare) 2Sam 13:25 ; Jer 18:18 ; Jonah 1:14 . In an imprecation: Gen 49:4 אַלתּֿוֺתַר have not thou the excellency! Psa 109:12 ; Job 3:4 , 6 . Sometimes strengthened by נָא : Gen 13:8 ; 18:3 and elsewhere ( b ) without a verb, ( α ) 2Sam 1:21 let (there be) not dew & not rain upon you! Isa 62:6 ; Psa 83:1 . ( β ) used absolutely, in deprecation Gen 19:18 ; 2Sam 13:16 (see below אוֺדָה ) 2Kin 3:13 ; 4:16 ; 6:27 (see RVm: but possibly to be explained by Dr § 152 iii ; so Th Ke: hardly as Ew § 355 b ) Ruth 1:13 בְּנֹתַי אַל Nay , my daughters, compare Judg 19:23 ; ( γ ) after a preceding imperative Amos 5:14 ; Joel 2:13 ; Prov 8:10 , a jussive 27:2 , an infinitive absolute 27:2 . ( χ ) in poetry אַל sometimes expresses vividly the emotion or sympathy of the poet (see Dr § 56-8 ); Isa 2:9 לָהֶם וְאַלתִּֿשָּׂא and forgive them not! (with a touch of passion), Psa 41:3 ; Prov 3:25 ; Job 5:22 ; Psa 34:6 (but ᵑ6 ᵐ5 Ew Che here read וּפְנֵיכֶם , probably rightly); 50:3 a may our God come יֶ֫חֱשָרשׁ וְאַלֿ and not be silent! (the psalmist identifying himself with a spectator of the scene 50:2-3 ,b-c) 121:3 (contrast 121:4 לֹא ) Jer 46:6 +. b. once Prov 12:28 joined closely to a substantive (compare לֹא 2 b ) to express with emphasis its negation: In the way of righteousness is life, and in the pathway therecf אַלמָֿוֶת there is no-death! i.e. immortality. c. once Job 24:25 used in poetry as a substantive, And bring my words לְאַל to nought! — N.B. 1Sam 27:10 אַל הַיּוֺם, אַלמְּֿשַׁטְתֶּם with the perfect is against all analogy; and either אֶלמִֿי (with ᵐ5 . ᵑ9 ), or better אָן whither? (with ᵑ7 ᵑ6 : see 10:14 ) must be read.","rootNote":"a negative particle (akin to 3808 );","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 16 22","keyReferences":["1Chr 16 22","1Chr 16 22","1Chr 21 13","1Chr 22 13","1Chr 22 13","1Chr 28 20","1Chr 28 20","1Kgs 2 9"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":725,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 16 22","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַֽל","source":"hebrew","morph"